{
  "case_id": "2011-11-204",
  "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nTHOMAS C. GOLDSTEIN, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of Petitioners.\nMALCOLM L. STEWART, ESQ., Deputy Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting Petitioners.\nPAUL D. CLEMENT, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GOLDSTEIN: Mr. Chief Justice, may it please the Court: In the Fair Labor Standards Act, Congress directed the Secretary of Labor to quote/unquote \"define and delimit\" the statute's outside salesman exemption. By regulation, the Secretary provided that an outside salesman is one who makes sales rather than promoting sales by others. In further guidance, the Secretary elaborated that nonexempt promotion includes either, one, a conversation where there can be no commitment or, two, one where there will be no exchange with the employer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, is that consistent with the Government's argument? They argue, quote, \"an employee does not make a 'sale' for purposes of the 'outside salesman' exemption unless he actually transfers title to the property at issue.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Excuse me. I -- I don't agree that there's an agreement for transfer of title. Where there's a consignment, you give the property to somebody, and he says I will sell it to somebody if somebody will buy it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GOLDSTEIN: I'm sorry. So, your premise is that they are exempt to begin with? There -- I can tell you that there are a large number of employees who do work outside the workplace and are substantially more autonomous than are pharmaceutical detailers, who have to operate from very strict scripts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 15,
        "start": 15
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GOLDSTEIN: Those are not, but the example that I gave to Justice Kennedy would be, which is that there are outside buyers who do receive commissions. And remember, of course, that there are outside salesmen who do not receive commissions but are nonetheless exempt."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0000-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STEWART: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: It's common ground in this case that in order to be an outside salesman, an employee must make sales. And in theory there are two different ways in which Respondent could have attempted to establish that the PSRs in this case fit that criteria."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Department of Labor",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STEWART: But I think much the same thing could have been said about all the promotional workers that DOL has done with -- has dealt with in the past. That is, the premise, the justification for a company to hire a promotional worker, is that the promotional activities will increase the overall sales of the company, will either directly or indirectly set in motion a chain of events that leads people to buy the"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, do those employees work on commissions?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Did we have detailers in 1940?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "National Federation of Independent Small Business Legal Center",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the National Federation of Independent Small Business Legal Center has filed an amicus brief on Respondent's side"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Department of Labor",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STEWART: And the agency has regarded the application of its promotion sales regulations to the facts of this case as clear. That is, if you asked GSK's highest level management why does it make sense to employ detailers, they wouldn't say because they get these commitments from physicians which are of value to the company."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. CLEMENT)",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0002-0009",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We got summary judgment in our favor on the outside sales exemption."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are they paid commissions?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How's that different from a bonus that an employee gets? How is it any different than what most companies do in -- in giving a bonus at the end of the year?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If -- forget the transfer of title business, but if it's just -- we're requiring a transaction here. And we're drawing a line between people who do transactions and people who just advertise or make pitches or whatever you want to do it. That's perfectly consistent with the statute, isn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "PhRMA",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0002-0008",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "they've imposed, by taking this position in an amicus brief and asking for deference to it, massive liability on this industry. The PhRMA brief estimates it's billions of dollars."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Does the -- does the pharmaceutical company have a sales force? I mean, who sells to the wholesalers, the pharmacies, and the hospitals?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. CLEMENT",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0003-0000",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We all know that retroactive rulemaking is\n disfavored. Well, think about the consequences here.\n You have massive liability, between 4 and 6 years of\n effective time and a half, because of the way that the\n statute works. It has time and a half plus liquidated"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Let's pursue this for a\n second."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "THOMAS C. GOLDSTEIN",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Three quick points. First, if you read the\n transcript, you will see that my friend says that the\n nature of this job has changed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0003-0004",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "for the Petitioners: \"Sales volume is directly and\n exclusively driven by the number of prescriptions\n written by physicians, and plaintiffs' job was to\n encourage such prescriptions.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. GOLDSTEIN",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
      "evidence_id": "ev-57f0f655739d-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "firm commitment. That's what the Department says. And\n there is nothing in the definition in 3(k) that\n contradicts that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2011-11-204",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "57f0f655739db3c5aec3f82a8580018a81d115e138f3d1327d49a85c2e21de62",
